{
  "_comment": [
    "Secret redaction rules, shared by the hook (core/bin/prepare.jq) and the sender (judgment_core/redact.py). This file is the source.",
    "scripts/gen_redact.py derives core/bin/redact-compiled.json (what jq loads: every regex composed) from it.",
    "Redaction is by format, plus three short data lists: secretNames (a value after one of these names), sensitivePaths and",
    "sensitiveCommands (a tool call that touches one blanks its turn). Nothing here parses code, shell, or patches.",
    "Regexes use what Oniguruma and Python re agree on: (?<name>...) for a named group (p, when it is the first group: the text",
    "it holds is kept, when it starts the match);",
    "An identifier boundary also holds right after an escape a JSON string or a terminal writes before a word: \\n \\r \\t \\b \\f,",
    "\\uXXXX, and the m that ends an ANSI color code ([1m, [32m, ;31m).",
    "no ^ or $ (use (?<![\\s\\S]) and (?![\\s\\S]) for the ends of a whole value); [0-9] and [A-Za-z], not \\d and \\w;",
    "no (?i), because Oniguruma compiles it slowly and jq compiles a regex on every call. Words are spelled lower, UPPER, and Capitalized.",
    "Linear time: no repeat inside a repeat over characters both can take, and no two unbounded repeats over overlapping",
    "characters in a row (tests/test_latency.py feeds every rule pathological text in both layers).",
    "needs: a rule can match only text holding one of these literals. Both layers skip the regex otherwise. tests/test_redact.py checks it.",
    "pre: a small regex every match also matches; both layers skip the rule's regex when the text does not match it."
  ],
  "version": 4,
  "limits": {
    "_comment": [
      "Bounds on the work redaction does, so no input makes the hook slow (tests/test_latency.py).",
      "A rule runs over windows of the unchanged text: each `window` characters long, one every `step`. jq's global match counts each",
      "match's offset from the start of the string it is given, so short strings keep that linear. Text no longer than `window` is one",
      "window. A match is kept from every window that holds it whole. A match that reaches the end of a window that is not the last is",
      "seen whole by the next window when it starts at or after that window's start; when it starts before, it is longer than",
      "window - step characters and the event fails closed. A rule marked whole runs over all of the text, and fails when the text holds",
      "more than `most` of the literals it needs. More than `pairs` distinct finds in one event fail too, as does a prompt with more than",
      "`mentions` @ signs. A failure drops the event's text, as an invalid user regex does.",
      "A window of at most `dense` characters is matched globally (one regex compile; few enough matches that jq's offset counting",
      "costs little). A longer one is matched one distinct match at a time, each one's copies blanked first, so repeats cost one search.",
      "The hook allows `pairs` distinct finds an event: jq matches a long window once per distinct find. The sender's matching",
      "is linear (one finditer per rule and window, its finds kept as spans of the unchanged text), so it allows `sender_pairs`.",
      "JSON nested in a string deeper than its rules read (a string holding \\\\\\\" ) is decoded, up to `depth` layers; what each",
      "layer holds is replaced as encoded where it sits. Deeper nesting, or a find whose encoding is not in the text, fails."
    ],
    "window": 16384,
    "step": 8192,
    "pairs": 128,
    "mentions": 256,
    "dense": 8192,
    "sender_pairs": 4096,
    "depth": 4
  },
  "settings": {
    "_comment": [
      "The redaction settings a project's tracing.json may hold, and what a malformed one does. Each is a list of strings.",
      "rule: it adds rules, so a value that is not a list of strings fails the rule set closed (every event loses its text).",
      "trim: it only takes rules or finds away, so anything that is not a nonempty string in a list is skipped.",
      "Both layers, and every adapter that forwards a project's settings, read the keys from here."
    ],
    "redactPatterns": "rule",
    "redactPaths": "rule",
    "redactCommands": "rule",
    "redactNames": "rule",
    "redactAllow": "trim",
    "redactDisable": "trim"
  },
  "patterns": [
    {
      "id": "private_key",
      "needs": [
        "PRIVATE KEY"
      ],
      "re": "-----BEGIN[A-Z0-9 ]{0,30}PRIVATE KEY(?: BLOCK)?-----(?:[\\s\\S]{0,16384}?-----END[A-Z0-9 ]{0,30}PRIVATE KEY(?: BLOCK)?-----|[A-Za-z0-9+/=\\s\\\\:,-]{0,16384})",
      "whole": true,
      "most": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "jwt",
      "needs": [
        "eyJ"
      ],
      "re": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]*"
    },
    {
      "id": "anthropic_key",
      "needs": [
        "sk-ant-"
      ],
      "re": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))sk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "openai_key",
      "needs": [
        "sk-"
      ],
      "re": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))sk-(?:proj-|svcacct-|admin-)?(?=[A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,256}?[A-Za-z0-9_]{16})[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}",
      "pre": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))sk-"
    },
    {
      "id": "aws_access_key_id",
      "needs": [
        "AKIA",
        "ASIA",
        "ABIA",
        "ACCA"
      ],
      "re": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))(?:AKIA|ASIA|ABIA|ACCA)[0-9A-Z]{16}(?![0-9A-Za-z])"
    },
    {
      "id": "github_token",
      "needs": [
        "ghp_",
        "gho_",
        "ghu_",
        "ghs_",
        "ghr_"
      ],
      "re": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "github_pat",
      "needs": [
        "github_pat_"
      ],
      "re": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{22,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "slack_token",
      "needs": [
        "xoxa-",
        "xoxb-",
        "xoxp-",
        "xoxr-",
        "xoxs-",
        "xoxe-"
      ],
      "re": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))xox[abprse]-(?=[A-Za-z0-9-]{0,255}[0-9])[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "slack_webhook",
      "needs": [
        "hooks.slack.com/services/"
      ],
      "re": "(?<p>hooks\\.slack\\.com/services/)[A-Za-z0-9/_-]{20,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "google_api_key",
      "needs": [
        "AIza"
      ],
      "re": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}(?![0-9A-Za-z_-])"
    },
    {
      "id": "stripe_key",
      "needs": [
        "sk_live_",
        "sk_test_",
        "rk_live_",
        "rk_test_"
      ],
      "re": "(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))(?:sk|rk)_(?:live|test)_[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}"
    },
    {
      "_comment": [
        "Any nonempty password, %-encoded included. Only a whole placeholder before the @ is exempt (${X}, $X, ****, xxx, password, ...)."
      ],
      "id": "url_password",
      "needs": [
        "://"
      ],
      "re": "(?<p>(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9+.-])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]{1,20}://[^\\s/:@'\\\"<>\\[\\]]{0,128}:)(?!(?:\\[REDACTED:[A-Za-z0-9_:.-]{1,128}\\](?:#[0-9]{1,6})?|\\$\\{[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}\\}|\\$[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}|\\{\\{\\s{0,4}[.A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.]{0,127}\\s{0,4}\\}\\}|%[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}%|\\*{1,64}|x{3,64}|X{3,64}|password|PASSWORD|Password|pass|PASS|Pass|passwd|PASSWD|Passwd|pwd|PWD|Pwd|secret|SECRET|Secret|changeme|CHANGEME|Changeme)@)[^\\s/@'\\\"<>]+(?=@)"
    },
    {
      "id": "authorization_header",
      "needs": [
        "uthorization",
        "UTHORIZATION",
        "-key",
        "-Key",
        "-KEY",
        "-token",
        "-Token",
        "-TOKEN"
      ],
      "re": "(?<p>(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))(?:(?:proxy|PROXY|Proxy)-(?:authorization|AUTHORIZATION|Authorization)|(?:authorization|AUTHORIZATION|Authorization)|(?:x|X)-(?:api|API|Api)-(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:api|API|Api)-(?:key|KEY|Key)|(?:x|X)-(?:auth|AUTH|Auth)-(?:token|TOKEN|Token))\\\\?[\\\"']?\\s{0,5}[:=]\\s{0,5}\\\\?[\\\"']?(?:(?:basic|BASIC|Basic|bearer|BEARER|Bearer|token|TOKEN|Token|digest|DIGEST|Digest|bot|BOT|Bot|apikey|APIKEY|Apikey)\\s+)?)(?!\\$|<|\\{\\{|%)(?=[A-Za-z._~+/=-]{0,255}[0-9+/=])[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]{12,}"
    },
    {
      "id": "bearer_token",
      "needs": [
        "bearer",
        "BEARER",
        "Bearer"
      ],
      "re": "(?<p>(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_-])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m))(?:bearer|BEARER|Bearer)\\s+)(?!\\$|<|\\{\\{|%)(?=[A-Za-z._~+/=-]{0,255}[0-9])[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]{16,}"
    }
  ],
  "secretNames": {
    "_comment": [
      "A value after one of these names is redacted, whatever it looks like. A name is lowercase parts joined by _; it matches",
      "each part lower, UPPER, or Capitalized, joined by _, -, ., or nothing (api_key: API_KEY, api-key, apiKey, ApiKey, apikey).",
      "It counts at an identifier boundary: after no letter or digit (db_password, --token), or at a camelCase hump (smtpPassword).",
      "Left out on purpose: key and auth (sort_key, s3 object keys, oauth), which only format rules redact, and authorization (authorization_header and bearer_token read headers).",
      "A project adds names with redactNames in .judgment/tracing.json."
    ],
    "names": [
      "password",
      "passwd",
      "pwd",
      "passphrase",
      "secret",
      "secret_key",
      "client_secret",
      "token",
      "api_key",
      "access_key",
      "private_key",
      "credential",
      "credentials"
    ],
    "assignment": {
      "_comment": [
        "secret_assignment, in text: {names} at an identifier boundary, an optional closing quote, backtick, or Markdown ** (the",
        "quote escaped any number of times, as nested JSON writes it), : or = (also := and =>), an optional closing ** before a blank, then the value: quoted (up to its quote, a newline, a comma, or a",
        "backslash; not starting with a blank or + ) ; ] }, which follow a string that just closed: \"password: \" + pw), or bare",
        "(up to a blank, a quote, a comma, ; ) ] } or a backslash; not starting with = [ { ( or :).",
        "Only the value is replaced. A value that is already a placeholder is left alone."
      ],
      "id": "secret_assignment",
      "re": "(?<p>(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9])|(?<=\\\\[nrtbf])|(?<=\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4})|(?<=[\\[;][0-9]m)|(?<=[\\[;][0-9][0-9]m)|(?<=[a-z0-9])(?=[A-Z])){names}\\\\{0,31}(?:[\"'`]|\\*{1,2})?[^\\S\\n]{0,32}(?::=|=>|[:=])(?:\\*{1,2}(?=[^\\S\\n]))?[^\\S\\n]{0,32}\\\\{0,31}[\"'`]?)(?!\\[REDACTED:)(?:(?<=\")[^\"\\s,\\\\+);\\]}][^\"\\n,\\\\]*|(?<=')[^'\\s,\\\\+);\\]}][^'\\n,\\\\]*|(?<=`)[^`\\s,\\\\+);\\]}][^`\\n,\\\\]*|(?<![\"'`])[^\\s\"'`,;\\\\)\\]}=\\[{(:][^\\s\"'`,;\\\\)\\]}]*)"
    },
    "field": {
      "_comment": [
        "secret_field, in structured values: a member whose key ends in one of the names (at the same boundaries) loses its",
        "nonempty string value. It runs over the compact JSON of the event's text fields in both layers, as jq writes it."
      ],
      "id": "secret_field",
      "re": "(?<p>(?<=[{,])\"[^\"\\\\\\n]{0,128}?(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9])|(?<=[a-z0-9])(?=[A-Z])){names}\":\")(?!\\[REDACTED:)(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)+(?:(?=\")|(?![\\s\\S]))",
      "needs_suffix": "\":\""
    },
    "allow": [
      "str",
      "string",
      "String",
      "None",
      "null",
      "nil",
      "undefined",
      "bool",
      "boolean",
      "int",
      "true",
      "false",
      "True",
      "False",
      "Optional[str"
    ]
  },
  "env": {
    "_comment": [
      "The value of each environment variable whose name looks secret is replaced literally wherever it appears: the whole value,",
      "and each line of a value that spans lines. name_re runs over the names, one per line, and matches each secret name whole.",
      "A name matches when it is JUDGMENT_API_KEY, or holds KEY, TOKEN, SECRET, PASSWORD, PASSWD, CREDENTIAL, PRIVATE, or AUTH",
      "(not as part of AUTHOR, KEYBOARD, KEYMAP, KEYCHAIN, MONKEY, TURKEY), and does not end in a suffix that names a location or a",
      "setting (_PATH, _FILE, _DIR, _SOCK, _URL, _HOST, _ID, _TOKENS, _LIMIT, ...): those values are paths, hosts, ids, or numbers.",
      "Any value (or line) of min_length or more characters with something other than whitespace in it is replaced, whatever its",
      "shape. A shorter one is not: replacing every 4-character run such as 2024 in all text would destroy ordinary text. Known limit.",
      "Each event also records env_found: {name, field} for every such value its raw text held, whatever rule replaced it",
      "and even when its rules failed. The sender reads it to know which env values the hook's text depended on."
    ],
    "name_re": "(?<![^\\n])(?:JUDGMENT_API_KEY(?![^\\n])|(?=[^\\n]*?(?:token|TOKEN|Token|secret|SECRET|Secret|password|PASSWORD|Password|passwd|PASSWD|Passwd|credential|CREDENTIAL|Credential|private|PRIVATE|Private|auth(?!or(?!iz))|AUTH(?!OR(?!IZ))|Auth(?!or(?!iz))|(?<![Mm][Oo][Nn])(?<![Tt][Uu][Rr])(?:key|KEY|Key)(?![Bb][Oo][Aa][Rr][Dd]|[Mm][Aa][Pp]|[Cc][Hh][Aa][Ii][Nn])))(?![^\\n]*(?:_PATH|_path|_FILE|_file|_DIR|_dir|_SOCK|_sock|_SOCKET|_socket|_HOST|_host|_PORT|_port|_URL|_url|_URI|_uri|_ID|_id|_MODE|_mode|_TYPE|_type|_NAME|_name|_USER|_user|_USERNAME|_username|_ENABLED|_enabled|_DISABLED|_disabled|_TIMEOUT|_timeout|_TOKENS|_tokens|_LIMIT|_limit|_REGION|_region)(?![^\\n]))[^\\n]+)",
    "min_length": 8
  },
  "sensitive": {
    "_comment": [
      "A tool call that runs one of these commands, or touches one of these paths, blanks its whole turn (commands are checked first).",
      "keys: the tool input members (at any depth) whose strings are read: paths, commands, and patches (Codex's apply_patch",
      "arrives as {\"input\": patch}). A string tool input is a command.",
      "Paths: every string under those keys, and each @word of the prompt, is split into tokens at the split characters.",
      "A token is sensitive when its last component (after the last / or :) matches one of a rule's globs and none of its",
      "! globs. A glob holding a / matches the token's last components (.kube/config). * is any run of characters but / and :,",
      "? one such character. A token is a mention: a read, a write, a patch header, or a word in a patch's body all count. Over-blanking",
      "is the accepted direction: it loses one turn's text and never leaks.",
      "Commands: each command string is matched on its own. A command counts at the start of the string or after ; & | ( { `",
      "or a newline, behind an optional sudo (command.prefix). One with --help, -h, or --version before the next ; & | ( ) { `",
      "or newline does not count (command.unless): the help check stops where a command can start, so it is linear.",
      "glob: how a project's redactPaths glob becomes a regex, one character at a time. There * is any run of characters, / included."
    ],
    "keys": {
      "file_path": "path",
      "filePath": "path",
      "path": "path",
      "paths": "path",
      "file": "path",
      "files": "path",
      "filename": "path",
      "notebook_path": "path",
      "target_file": "path",
      "target_notebook": "path",
      "absolute_path": "path",
      "relative_path": "path",
      "source": "path",
      "destination": "path",
      "command": "command",
      "cmd": "command",
      "commands": "command",
      "script": "command",
      "input": "patch",
      "patch": "patch",
      "diff": "patch"
    },
    "split": [
      " ",
      "\t",
      "\n",
      "\r",
      "\f",
      "\u000b",
      "\"",
      "'",
      "`",
      ";",
      "|",
      "&",
      "<",
      ">",
      "(",
      ")",
      "="
    ],
    "mention": {
      "split": [
        " ",
        "\t",
        "\n",
        "\r",
        "\f",
        "\u000b",
        "("
      ],
      "end": [
        ",",
        ";",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    "glob": {
      "*": "[^\\n]*",
      "?": "[^\\n]",
      ".": "\\.",
      "\\": "\\\\",
      "+": "\\+",
      "^": "\\^",
      "$": "\\$",
      "(": "\\(",
      ")": "\\)",
      "[": "\\[",
      "]": "\\]",
      "{": "\\{",
      "}": "\\}",
      "|": "\\|"
    },
    "command": {
      "prefix": "(?:(?<![\\s\\S])|(?<=[;&|\\n(`{]))[^\\S\\n]*(?:(?:then|do|else|time|exec|command|nohup|!)[^\\S\\n]+)?(?:[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=[^\\s;&|`(){\"']*[^\\S\\n]+)*(?:sudo(?:[^\\S\\n]+-[A-Za-z]+(?:[^\\S\\n]+[^\\s;&|`)-][^\\s;&|`)]*)?)*[^\\S\\n]+)?(?:(?:/(?:usr/)?(?:local/)?bin/)?(?:ba|z|da|k)?sh[^\\S\\n]+-[A-Za-z]*c[^\\S\\n]+[\"']?)?(?:[^\\s;&|`(){\"']*/)?",
      "unless": "(?![^;&|\\n)`({]*[^\\S\\n](?:--help|-h|--version)(?![^\\s;&|)`\"']))"
    },
    "paths": [
      {
        "id": "dotenv",
        "globs": [
          ".env*",
          "?*.env",
          "!.env.example",
          "!.env.sample",
          "!.env.template",
          "!.env.dist",
          "!.env.default",
          "!.env.defaults",
          "!.env.schema",
          "!example.env"
        ],
        "examples": [
          ".env",
          ".env.local",
          "app/.env.production",
          ".envrc",
          "HEAD:.env",
          ".env~",
          ".env.local~",
          "prod.env",
          ".env-prod"
        ],
        "not": [
          ".env.example",
          "src/environment.ts",
          "docs/env.md",
          "example.env"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ssh_private_key",
        "globs": [
          "id_rsa*",
          "id_dsa*",
          "id_ecdsa*",
          "id_ed25519*",
          "!*.pub"
        ],
        "examples": [
